# CHAMPION NIGHT env (2026-09-08; Plan_2026-09-08_Champion_Night.md = the registration; PI decisions 2026-09-08 ~05:45Z:
# "a v6e-16 between US and Mumbai through churns; keep all seven arms; 30k steps with contingencies for more if the score
# keeps increasing at the end"). Seven one-variable arms of the DEC-w384 champion recipe (A5's: FPA k1 + RI sigma 1, no
# digit aug, the field regime, 30k SOT steps, the 512-puzzle monitor + earliest tie): C0 C1 C2 = seeds 0/1/2 · C3 = the
# ONLINE position orbit (50k) · C4 = set attention over the fields · C5 = w192 · C6 = the calibrated commit head (50k).
# The registered EXTENSION rule (R-CH-EXT): an arm whose selected grid sits inside the last 4k steps of its budget is
# extended ONCE by +20k (labeled EXTENDED.txt), then re-selected. Shape: ONE spot v6e-16 (4 workers x 4 chips), hunted
# across the US zones first and Mumbai last, re-hunted through churn (no 32, no 8: the static 4x4 map is the campaign).
# 4x4 map (balanced by the measured hours): w0 C0 C4 · w1 C1 C2 · w2 C6 · w3 [rider] C3 C5 (pole ~ 26 h + extensions); every worker preflights.
# Walls ~ 2 nights (~ 24-30 h) at $13.64/h US ($16 Mumbai) ~ $330-480 + weather; cap launch + 36 h (the knob).
# The sync-policy A/B rider runs FIRST on w3 (SYNC-AB marker). The previous (frontier) env is in git (commit 4c7f5bb).
POD=qhrrn2-pod2
ZONES="us-east1-d us-east5-b us-central1-a us-central2-b us-west1-c asia-south1-c"
ACCEL=v6e-16
ACCEL_LIST="v6e-16"
BIG_MAX_STRIKES=99
R_TAG=champ
R_D=384
R_STEPS=30000
ARMS="C0 C1 C2 C3 C4 C5 C6"
CHAIN_SCRIPT=tools/chain_champ.sh
CHAIN_EXTRA_ENV="C1_MON=2000 SELF_TEARDOWN=1 C1_WAIT_PASSES=900"
WALL=30600
SENTINEL=CHAIN-CHAMP-COMPLETE
GCS=gs://qhrrn2-rescue/champ
FINAL_OBJ=champ_final.tgz
CANARY_CKPT=runs/pretrain6_d24/ckpt_latest.pkl
